const ST_CAPTION: Array[&str, 79] = ["The display says go. Only the display starts a frame.", "Render tells the Presenter, and gives it a small budget to commit.", "Render waits, but only that long. Past it, it draws Scene A again.", "The Host posts what you did. It starts nothing itself.", "The Presenter moves your body at once, inside the frame you stand in.", "Your input goes to the Authority: encoded, even locally. It costs almost nothing.", "The Presenter waits for this tick, which keeps others at zero lag. Only inside its budget.", "A 60 Hz step is due. The Authority moves beings, platforms and timers. This copy wins.", "The world's mail goes to the stranger's code, with a time budget.", "The World program runs. If it overruns, nobody below waits for it.", "It answers with requests. It cannot touch the Authority's data directly.", "The Authority takes them, and decides what they do.", "It commits. The latest state goes out. A newer one would replace it unread.", "The Presenter has its tick, inside the budget. Most frames go this way.", "It checks your body, places everyone else, and writes Scene B.", "Scene B names shapes in the library. It holds no copies: built once, shared by all.", "Sound commands go in Audio's queue. Audio runs on its own clock and never waits.", "The Presenter commits by handing Scene B over. Nothing is copied.", "Render has its scene.", "Now the head pose: as late as possible, so your head always feels right.", "The eye is composed last: the platform, your body on it, your head.", "Render draws both eyes. Most of the frame is here, and in the wait for the next.", "Meanwhile, on spare cores, Arrival finishes a tower. It shares no deadline with the frame.", "The finished tower joins the library, built once. Nobody can change it after this.", "Scene A goes back to the Presenter as the next spare. A frame allocates no new scene.", "Render presents, and sleeps until the display says go again, 13.9 ms after the last.", "The Host posts the click. It has no idea what you clicked.", "The Presenter looks at the scene you are seeing now, not at the Authority's latest.", "It tests your ray against the library's shapes. The bell was there, so you hit it.", "The answer travels as an event: reliable, in order, never replaced by a newer one.", "The Authority does not test the ray again. That matters only against cheating. Open.", "The click becomes mail for the world, with a time budget.", "The stranger's code decides what a click means. The browser has no idea.", "It asks for a swing and a sound.", "The Authority checks the requests and applies them.", "The bell now swings in the copy that wins.", "The swing goes out as state. If two snapshots queue, only the newest counts.", "The sound goes out as an event, because it must not be lost.", "The Presenter hands it to Audio, placed where the bell is in your scene.", "The next commit shows the swing. Your head moved freely all this while.", "Mail goes to the World program, with its budget, as on any step.", "The stranger's code never returns.", "The budget runs out. The Authority does not wait: it moves on. This is the rule at work.", "Beings carry on with their last intents, so a villager keeps walking. Nothing new is decided.", "State goes out as usual.", "The picture goes on.", "Your head still feels right.", "Sound goes on.", "Mail waits. The world has stopped answering, and only the world.", "The browser can tell you. You can leave, because leaving is not the world's to refuse.", "The browser stops the World program. How to stop it mid-change without half-made state is open.", "You walk. The Presenter moves your body in the deck's frame, not the world's.", "The deck is rigid, so the ship's motion cannot correct your walking. In the model, 1,610 corrections a minute became 0.", "The ship's pose arrives as state, latest wins, about 100 ms old. A pilot you cannot foresee steers it.", "Render composes last: ship's pose, you on it, your head. An error in the ship moves you and the deck together.", "You near the exit, so now the ship is predicted forward, to show where the rail truly is.", "The world declared this gangway routine: docked, and crossing is what you are here to do.", "You step off. The crossing goes as an event, with where you were drawn.", "The Authority accepts the drawn pose, within 1 m. The player's view gets the benefit.", "While docked, a routine crossing gets 2 m of help toward the dock. 0 of 320 failed.", "A change of frame is an event, reliable, never state. Reported failures in other games cluster here.", "Your body moves to the dock's frame, keeping its place. Nothing pops.", "Had the ship been moving, this is a risky leap: no help. The model disagrees with the player 4.7% of the time.", "The world is told, as mail, so it can greet you or charge you the fare.", "The world declares a tower: only its id and place. Nothing is built yet.", "The Authority records that it exists. It can be stood near before it can be seen.", "The Presenter learns of it as an event.", "The tower joins Arrival's list, ordered by how near you are. You move; the order moves.", "Arrival checks the bake cache. It is the cache's one writer, so nothing can collide.", "Not there, so it is fetched on the content channel, which cannot stall state or events.", "Meanwhile frames go on. Nobody in the frame knows or cares.", "On spare cores, Arrival decodes. Different objects run side by side.", "It builds the mesh and the collision shape, each once. Today this is done twice.", "It writes the bake cache, so the next visit starts here.", "The tower joins the library. From now on nobody can change it, so anyone may read it.", "The Authority picks up the same collision shape. One copy, not one for each physics world.", "Render uploads to the GPU under a budget each frame. This hand-over is the risk in a huge world.", "After a few frames the tower is resident.", "The next scene names it, and you see it. No frame ever waited."];
